Subject: [PATCH] The lower menu as quick access (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On the 3DS remaster's lower menu, a tap on a button does what it says at
once, and leaving what it opened leaves the menu too:

- A tap opens the menu straight on the button with the press's sound
  (the menu's opening sound is X's: field_control.c asks
  StartMenu_PortTapOpening). What the tap opened, left (B, or the bag's
  button again; the party, the trainer card, the Pokédex, the options, the
  Town Map, the save's question answered no), leaves the menu: back to
  walking. Opened with X, the menu comes back as on the DS.
- The panel keeps the tab chosen last: the map, the Pokétch, or the bag as
  the player left it. The bag's tab shows the bag's picture (the platform
  keeps the lower screen's picture when the bag settles and as it's left:
  NitroPort_LowerMenuKeepPicture); a tap on it opens the bag.
- BAG: the picture shown at once, the bag itself once it's whole (the
  upper screen keeping the field, the menu kept on meanwhile:
  NitroPort_LowerMenuKeepShown); B or BAG puts it away the same way, the
  picture as it was left kept on while the field comes back. The first
  time (no picture yet) the lower screen is kept as it is instead.
- From the bag, MAP shows the map in the panel at once (the port draws
  it), POKéTCH the Pokétch as it was when the bag came (its picture) till
  the field's back; the button tapped is lit at once.
- MAP shows the map; only a double tap on it (NitroPort_LowerMenuPressDouble)
  opens the Town Map app, or A on it with the map shown in the menu opened
  with X. A tap on the map does nothing.
